==German==
{{wikipedia|Pronomen|lang=de}}
===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/pʁoˈnoːmən/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Pronomen.ogg|audio|lang=de}}

===Etymology===
From Latin {{l|la|pronomen}}.

===Noun===
{{de-noun|n|Pronomens|Pronomen|pl2=Pronomina}}
# {{context|grammar|lang=de}} [[pronoun]] or [[determiner]], [[pronominal]] [[adjective]]

====Usage notes====
The English word ''pronoun'' is used with a different meaning than ''Pronomen''. "[[ours]]" is a possessive pronoun, but "[[our]]" is a possessive adjective. In German, however, both kinds of words are called ''Pronomen''. The grammatical difference can be expressed e.g. by calling "ours" a ''substantivisches Pronomen'' and "our" an ''adjektivisches Pronomen''.

